cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it, and cite the dataset and paper listed under references."
title: "Expected Goals Lab: a transparent expected-goals study on Wyscout open event data"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Poswell
    given-names: Aiden
abstract: >-
  A one-season, five-league study of how much shot location explains the chance of a goal and
  whether the provider's body-part tag adds predictive value, with chronological partitions,
  one score-held-out evaluation and a development-only audit of shot-origin coordinates.
  Research code and aggregate results only; no provider data are redistributed.
keywords:
  - football
  - expected goals
  - xG
  - sports analytics
